    {
      "id": "1f4971b5-847d-5c9c-a641-8d1770f13249",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -620,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 500,
        "height": 860,
        "content": "## Book property viewings and send reminders\n\nLet buyers book a viewing from your website without back-and-forth emails \u2014 the workflow only accepts free slots in your diary.\n\n### How it works\n1. A form posts the request (name, email, listing, date/time) to the **webhook**.\n2. The request is checked against your opening days and hours and minimum notice.\n3. **Google Calendar** availability is checked, including a travel buffer.\n4. Free slot: the event is created, logged in **Viewings**, and the buyer gets a confirmation (you are in BCC).\n5. Busy slot: the closest free times over the next days are emailed and returned to the form.\n6. Every hour, booked viewings starting within 24h get a reminder email.\n\n### Setup\n- Connect **Google Calendar**, **Gmail** and **Google Sheets** credentials.\n- Fill the **Config** node: Sheet ID, calendar ID, time zone, hours, durations.\n- Uses one Google Sheet with three tabs \u2014 **Leads**, **Listings**, **Viewings** \u2014 shared by the whole Real Estate Automation Kit (column list in the README).\n\n### Customization tips\n- Change `viewingMinutes`, `bufferMinutes` and `workingDays` to match your agency.\n- Adjust `reminderHoursBefore` for earlier reminders."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "1b8bc5bb-92f7-5306-9eba-7e65ebd1d2c0",
      "name": "Section 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -60,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 860,
        "content": "## 1. Entry points\nA web form books viewings; an hourly schedule sends reminders."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
